From: Cygwin Maintainers
Subject: Main Cygwin-specific adaptations for bash

This patch provides Cygwin-specific functionality:
- igncr option: Ignore carriage returns in input (for Windows line endings)
- completion_strip_exe: Strip .exe suffix when foo and foo.exe are same file
- IMP() macro: Handle DLL import symbol differences between x86 and x86_64
- UNC path handling: Fast path for //server names in completion
- Pipe fd relocation: Move pipe fds above 2 for non-Cygwin child compatibility
- Various fixes for Cygwin environment

NOTE: This patch was adapted from bash 5.2 to bash 5.1. Line numbers may need
adjustment. Review and test carefully before applying.

=== Key Features ===

1. IGNCR Option (set -o igncr / shopt igncr)
   - Strips carriage returns from input streams
   - Useful when dealing with Windows-style line endings
   - Implemented in: input.c, parse.y, subst.c, builtins/read.def, builtins/set.def

2. completion_strip_exe (shopt completion_strip_exe)
   - When completing "foo", if foo.exe exists and is the same file, show just "foo"
   - Default: on
   - Implemented in: bashline.c, builtins/shopt.def

3. IMP() Macro
   - Handles Cygwin DLL import naming differences
   - x86_64: __imp_##x
   - x86: _imp__##x
   - Used in function pointer comparisons with readline functions

4. UNC Path Fast Path
   - //server paths are assumed valid without slow stat() timeout
   - Improves tab completion performance

5. Pipe FD Relocation
   - Moves pipe file descriptors above 2 for command substitution
   - Prevents hangs when piping to non-Cygwin children

=== Files Modified ===

bashline.c:
- Add IMP() macro definition
- Add completion_strip_exe variable
- Add IMP() checks for readline function comparisons
- Add .exe stripping in command completion
- Add UNC path fast path in test_for_directory

builtins/read.def:
- Remove unnecessary io.h include
- Remove O_TEXT setmode call
- Add igncr support in read loop

builtins/set.def:
- Add igncr option
- Add interactive_only field to prevent non-interactive shell breakage
- Add set_minus_o_option_maybe wrapper

builtins/shopt.def:
- Add completion_strip_exe option

config-top.h:
- Enable SYS_BASHRC (/etc/bash.bashrc)

doc/Makefile.in:
- Enable builtins.1 man page installation

doc/bash.1, doc/bashref.texi:
- Document completion_strip_exe option

doc/builtins.1:
- Fix man page path reference

general.c:
- Include sys/cygwin.h
- Use CCP_ABSOLUTE flag in cygwin_conv_path

input.c:
- Define igncr variable
- Add igncr support in buffered_getchar

lib/sh/pathphys.c:
- Use realpath() on Cygwin for reliability

lib/sh/tmpfile.c:
- Additional file_iswdir check

mksyntax.c, support/bashversion.c:
- Move extern declarations for cleaner compilation

parse.y:
- Add igncr support in yy_string_get

subst.c:
- Add igncr support in read_comsub
- Relocate pipe fds above 2 for command substitution

support/mkversion.sh:
- Disable automatic build number increment

variables.c:
- Add void return type to sv_home

=== Application ===

This patch should be applied after the smaller config-top.h patches.
Some hunks may need manual adjustment for bash 5.1 differences.

To apply:
  cd /path/to/bash-5.1
  patch -p1 < cygwin-patches/50-cygwin.patch

For the full original patch content, see:
  /usr/src/bash-5.2.21-1.src/bash-5.2-cygwin.patch

